# Axb Optimus Site

> The public GitHub Pages site for Axb-Optimus, the humanoid built around predictive echo.

## Purpose
Explain the site as the public face of the robot repo, not the control loop itself. Source: fitzyracing1/axb-optimus-site.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Open the Pages site.
2. Read what Axb-Optimus is.
3. Follow the link to the control-loop repo if you want the code.

## Key ideas
- Pages site (the public page)
- Axb-Optimus (the named robot)
- Predictive echo (guess, act, hear, correct)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/axb-optimus-site
show_site()
point_to_axb_optimus()
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. show_site() → “open the public page”
2. point_to_axb_optimus() → “send readers to the robot repo”

## Decisions the program makes
- If a visitor wants the story → stay on the site
- If a visitor wants the loop → send them to axb-optimus

## What a person would notice
A public page in front of the robot code.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open the Pages site, or the axb-optimus source.
